    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the culture thing but at the end of the day business is about being competitive. if my competitors are cutting costs and moving faster because they aren't carrying the weight of a huge, expensive human staff, i'm the one losing. isn't it just a matter of progress? like, isn't it inevitable that inefficient manual labor gets replaced by more efficient tech? feels like you're trying to make it sound like a moral dilemma when it's really just basic economics.",
